--- task
id: a06
dataset: attribution
kind: an aggregate of an aggregate
answer: fewest
composition: an aggregate of an aggregate: edition 2 returns the per-identity counts and leaves the mean and the maximum to the caller

--- intent
What is the average number of touchpoints per identity, and the largest number any one identity has? Return them as `mean` and `largest`.

--- edition3
query touchpoints_per_identity() {
  match { from { match { $t touchpointByIdentity $x } return { $x, count($t) as n } } }
  return { avg($n) as mean, max($n) as largest }
}

--- edition3
query touchpoints_per_identity() {
  match { from { match { $x: ExternalID  $t touchpointByIdentity $x } return { $x, count($t) as n } } }
  return { avg($n) as mean, max($n) as largest }
}
